261:Our argument is largely based on the resolution lower bound of Beame and Pitassi \cite{beame}, which can be used to establish the hardness of instances from the random $k$-{\SAT} model.
262:In order to use that result, we need to show that most instances from the community attachment model have certain \emph{sparsity} properties used by the proof.
